# Controller Pattern

Controllers handle HTTP requests and responses, mapping between HTTP and domain layers.

## File Structure

```
rest/{entity-name}/
├── controllers/
│   └── {entity}.controller.ts  # All controller methods in ONE file
├── dtos/
│   ├── {entity}.dto.ts         # Response DTO
│   ├── create-{entity}.dto.ts  # Create request DTO
│   └── update-{entity}.dto.ts  # Update request DTO
├── mappers/
│   └── {entity}.mapper.ts      # Entity ↔ DTO mapper
└── routes.ts                   # Route definitions
```

## Controller Implementation Pattern

### Controller File (`controllers/{entity}.controller.ts`)

**IMPORTANT:** All controller methods for an entity go in ONE file.

```typescript
import type { Request, Response } from 'express';
import type { Usecases } from '@/usecases/index.js';
import type { AppContext } from '@/libs/context/index.js';
import type { EntityDto } from '../dtos/{entity}.dto.js';
import type { CreateEntityDto } from '../dtos/create-{entity}.dto.js';
import type { UpdateEntityDto } from '../dtos/update-{entity}.dto.js';
import { toDto } from '../mappers/{entity}.mapper.js';

export const initEntityControllers = (usecases: Usecases) => {
  
  const create = async (
    req: Request<any, EntityDto, CreateEntityDto> & { context: AppContext },
    res: Response<EntityDto>,
  ) => {
    const entity = await usecases.entity.create(req.context, {
      field: req.body.field,
    });

    const entityDto = toDto(entity);
    res.status(201).json(entityDto);
  };

  const getAll = async (
    req: Request<any, EntityDto[]> & { context: AppContext },
    res: Response<EntityDto[]>,
  ) => {
    const entities = await usecases.entity.getAll(req.context);
    const entitiesDto = entities.map(toDto);
    res.json(entitiesDto);
  };

  const getById = async (
    req: Request<{ id: string }, EntityDto> & { context: AppContext },
    res: Response<EntityDto>,
  ) => {
    const entity = await usecases.entity.getById(req.context, {
      id: req.params.id || '',
    });

    if (!entity) {
      return res.status(404).json({ message: 'Entity not found' } as any);
    }

    const entityDto = toDto(entity);
    res.json(entityDto);
  };

  const update = async (
    req: Request<{ id: string }, EntityDto, UpdateEntityDto> & { context: AppContext },
    res: Response<EntityDto>,
  ) => {
    const entity = await usecases.entity.update(req.context, {
      id: req.params.id || '',
      field: req.body.field,
    });

    const entityDto = toDto(entity);
    res.json(entityDto);
  };

  const deleteEntity = async (
    req: Request<{ id: string }> & { context: AppContext },
    res: Response<void>,
  ) => {
    await usecases.entity.delete(req.context, {
      id: req.params.id || '',
    });

    res.status(204).send();
  };

  return {
    create,
    getAll,
    getById,
    update,
    delete: deleteEntity,
  };
};

export type EntityControllers = ReturnType<typeof initEntityControllers>;
```

**Key Points:**
- Export `init{Entity}Controllers` factory function
- Takes `Usecases` as parameter (dependency injection)
- All controller methods in ONE file
- Each method extracts data from HTTP request
- Maps DTO fields to use case inputs
- Calls use case through `req.context`
- Maps entity to DTO using mapper
- Sets appropriate HTTP status codes
- Returns controller object with all methods
- Export type using `ReturnType<typeof ...>`

## HTTP Status Codes

- `200 OK` - Successful GET, PUT (default for `res.json()`)
- `201 Created` - Successful POST
- `204 No Content` - Successful DELETE
- `400 Bad Request` - Invalid input (caught in error handler)
- `401 Unauthorized` - Not authenticated
- `403 Forbidden` - Not authorized
- `404 Not Found` - Resource not found
- `500 Internal Server Error` - Server error (caught in error handler)

## Routes File (`routes.ts`)

```typescript
import { Router } from 'express';
import { initEntityControllers } from './controllers/{entity}.controller.js';
import type { Usecases } from '@/usecases/index.js';

export const initEntityRoutes = (usecases: Usecases) => {
  const controllers = initEntityControllers(usecases);
  const router = Router();

  router.get('/', controllers.getAll as any);
  router.get('/:id', controllers.getById as any);
  router.post('/', controllers.create as any);
  router.put('/:id', controllers.update as any);
  router.delete('/:id', controllers.delete as any);

  return router;
};
```

## DTOs (Data Transfer Objects)

### Response DTO (`dtos/{entity}.dto.ts`)

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

export const EntityDtoSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().uuid(),
  field: z.string(),
  createdAt: z.string().datetime(),
  updatedAt: z.string().datetime(),
});

export type EntityDto = z.infer<typeof EntityDtoSchema>;
```

### Create Request DTO (`dtos/create-{entity}.dto.ts`)

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

export const CreateEntityDtoSchema = z.object({
  field: z.string().min(1),
});

export type CreateEntityDto = z.infer<typeof CreateEntityDtoSchema>;
```

### Update Request DTO (`dtos/update-{entity}.dto.ts`)

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

export const UpdateEntityDtoSchema = z.object({
  field: z.string().min(1).optional(),
});

export type UpdateEntityDto = z.infer<typeof UpdateEntityDtoSchema>;
```

## DTO Mappers (`mappers/{entity}.mapper.ts`)

```typescript
import type { Entity } from '@/entities/{entity}/{entity}.js';
import type { EntityDto } from '../dtos/{entity}.dto.js';

export const toDto = (entity: Entity): EntityDto => {
  return {
    id: entity.id,
    field: entity.field,
    createdAt: entity.createdAt.toISOString(),
    updatedAt: entity.updatedAt.toISOString(),
  };
};
```

## Request Context

The `req.context` contains `AppContext` (config, logger, repositories, gateways, auth). Always pass `req.context` to use cases: `await usecases.entity.operation(req.context, input);`

## Checklist for New Controller

- [ ] Create `rest/{entity-name}/` directory
- [ ] Create `controllers/{entity}.controller.ts` with ALL methods in one file
- [ ] Create DTOs: `{entity}.dto.ts`, `create-{entity}.dto.ts`, `update-{entity}.dto.ts`
- [ ] Create `mappers/{entity}.mapper.ts` with `toDto` function
- [ ] Create `routes.ts` with route definitions
- [ ] Add to `rest/routes.ts` root router
- [ ] Use factory pattern: `init{Entity}Controllers`
- [ ] Pass `req.context` to use cases
- [ ] Map DTOs to use case inputs; map entities to DTOs
- [ ] Set correct HTTP status codes; handle 404 explicitly for getById
- [ ] Export controller types
